WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.826 --> 00:00:03.993
(upbeat string music)

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.588
- Hi, I'm Hannah, your
friendly neighborhood wine mom

00:00:09.588 --> 00:00:10.542
and if you're anything like me,

00:00:10.542 --> 00:00:12.002
you believe that a glass
of wine at eight p.m.

00:00:12.002 --> 00:00:13.187
makes you a better mom,

00:00:13.187 --> 00:00:15.022
so pour yourself a glass and let's talk.

00:00:15.022 --> 00:00:16.710
Tonight, we're gonna
drink some Chardonnay.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.369
And it's actually cold,

00:00:18.369 --> 00:00:20.626
which usually I just put ice cubes in it.

00:00:20.626 --> 00:00:21.935
Feeling pretty classy right now.

00:00:21.935 --> 00:00:22.991
So here's why I'm drinking tonight.

00:00:22.991 --> 00:00:23.949
Bringing it back.

00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:25.855
I have had the same song stuck in my head

00:00:25.855 --> 00:00:27.474
for the past three days,

00:00:27.474 --> 00:00:30.787
and it's not like a normal
song that's on the radio.

00:00:30.787 --> 00:00:33.726
It's a kids' TV show song,
and I'm not gonna hum it

00:00:33.726 --> 00:00:35.287
because one, we don't have the rights,

00:00:35.287 --> 00:00:37.833
and two, I don't wanna
get it stuck in your head.

00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:39.933
I wouldn't wish this upon my worst enemy.

00:00:39.933 --> 00:00:41.420
So on that note, let's talk about

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.639
the worst things about kid's TV shows.

00:00:43.639 --> 00:00:45.798
It's gonna be a 15 minute episode.

00:00:45.798 --> 00:00:47.949
So first, the reason why I'm drinking.

00:00:47.949 --> 00:00:50.313
The music in these kids' TV shows.

00:00:50.313 --> 00:00:52.940
It's so catchy, it's so repetitive.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.170
The tune is just so, like, sing song,

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.437
so I can just be in the same room

00:00:57.437 --> 00:00:59.503
as my son watching one of these shows

00:00:59.503 --> 00:01:01.182
and the whole song is stuck in my head

00:01:01.182 --> 00:01:02.633
for the next three weeks.

00:01:02.633 --> 00:01:04.420
Like I'll be at work and I'll like

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:07.375
inadvertently start
humming or even full on

00:01:07.375 --> 00:01:09.341
singing these songs and I'll be like:

00:01:09.341 --> 00:01:12.272
♫ If you have friends then you share

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.097
I look up and everybody's
looking at me like

00:01:14.097 --> 00:01:15.358
what the, what?

00:01:15.358 --> 00:01:18.140
Like I'll find myself on the
third week of having a song

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.541
stuck in my head singing myself to sleep,

00:01:20.541 --> 00:01:22.736
like rocking back and
forth in my bed like:

00:01:22.736 --> 00:01:27.188
♫ If you have friends you must share

00:01:27.188 --> 00:01:30.128
Goodnight, Hannah, sleep tight.

00:01:30.128 --> 00:01:31.906
So I really wish I had
a solution for this.

00:01:31.906 --> 00:01:33.750
There's no way around it, to be honest,

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.853
unless you're willing to
invest in a lifetime supply

00:01:35.853 --> 00:01:38.527
of earplugs, we're all kinda sunk.

00:01:38.527 --> 00:01:39.694
Next, Caillou.

00:01:40.615 --> 00:01:41.894
You all know what I'm talkin' about,

00:01:41.894 --> 00:01:44.477
but before I get started, just.

00:01:49.024 --> 00:01:50.210
Now I'm ready.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.801
Where do I even start
about this shitty ass kid?

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:55.191
First of all, if you
haven't seen it, don't.

00:01:55.191 --> 00:01:57.938
Don't Google it, don't
YouTube it, trust me.

00:01:57.938 --> 00:01:59.440
You've been warned, don't do it.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.817
Caillou is every parent's worst nightmare.

00:02:01.817 --> 00:02:05.607
Caillou is like this
weirdly ambiguous child,

00:02:05.607 --> 00:02:08.224
and I think they said
that they tried to make it

00:02:08.224 --> 00:02:11.036
to represent every child,
but it's like he's just

00:02:11.036 --> 00:02:15.258
a bald white kid, so way to
go on representation there.

00:02:15.258 --> 00:02:18.607
And he talks in this voice that's like:

00:02:18.607 --> 00:02:21.190
Mom, Rosie touched my painting.

00:02:22.891 --> 00:02:25.891
Mom, Rosie, she's touching my train.

00:02:27.459 --> 00:02:29.611
Even when he's happy
his voice is like that.

00:02:29.611 --> 00:02:32.896
Oh my gosh, Mom, I'm
having the best day ever.

00:02:32.896 --> 00:02:36.572
(high-pitched squealing)

00:02:36.572 --> 00:02:39.167
It's this voice that gets under your skin

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:42.007
and feels like spiders
crawling under your skin.

00:02:42.007 --> 00:02:45.405
And then the poor parents
are just like dead inside.

00:02:45.405 --> 00:02:49.752
You'll see Caillou be like
Mom, Rosie broke my toy.

00:02:49.752 --> 00:02:53.472
And the parent's just
like Caillou, it's okay.

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:55.844
Be nice to your sister.

00:02:55.844 --> 00:02:58.833
So basically all it does is
teach your kids to be a douche

00:02:58.833 --> 00:03:01.462
and it teaches the parents
that if your kid is a douche,

00:03:01.462 --> 00:03:03.179
you're just gonna die inside.

00:03:03.179 --> 00:03:05.506
So Caillou's mom, I know
you've got a stash of wine

00:03:05.506 --> 00:03:08.121
in your bedroom and you're
just like chugging that shit

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.669
the second the kids go to bed.

00:03:09.669 --> 00:03:10.751
This one's for you.

00:03:10.751 --> 00:03:13.391
Next, these shows suck you right in.

00:03:13.391 --> 00:03:16.536
These shows are made for
kids, but I swear they're also

00:03:16.536 --> 00:03:19.399
inadvertently made for parents to like

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:20.840
also get involved in these.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.782
Because my son will be watching
it, I'll be folding laundry

00:03:23.782 --> 00:03:27.417
on the other side of the
room, and he's like watching

00:03:27.417 --> 00:03:31.583
some show and they're asking
him oh what do I need to see?

00:03:31.583 --> 00:03:32.938
Glasses?

00:03:32.938 --> 00:03:33.771
A saw?

00:03:35.134 --> 00:03:36.383
A chair?

00:03:36.383 --> 00:03:38.807
Of course I'm gonna be like the glasses!

00:03:38.807 --> 00:03:41.420
And then my kid's like
Mom, I was guessing!

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:44.254
Even after my son has like
fully finished watching

00:03:44.254 --> 00:03:46.712
and left the room to go play in his room,

00:03:46.712 --> 00:03:50.115
I'll continue watching them for
like a good 20 more minutes.

00:03:50.115 --> 00:03:52.142
My husband actually walked
into the house one time

00:03:52.142 --> 00:03:55.347
and I was sitting on the couch
watching Dora the Explorer

00:03:55.347 --> 00:03:56.930
sitting there like.

00:04:00.225 --> 00:04:01.741
The map.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.545
And I just want a children's
show that I can ignore.

00:04:03.545 --> 00:04:05.545
Is that too much to ask?

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.741
Next, the adventures.

00:04:08.741 --> 00:04:11.779
The majority of these kids
TV shows involve the main

00:04:11.779 --> 00:04:14.212
child character going
on some crazy adventure

00:04:14.212 --> 00:04:16.996
to do something absolutely phenomenal

00:04:16.996 --> 00:04:18.557
to like save the world.

00:04:18.557 --> 00:04:20.093
I can't live up to that.

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:21.977
It's like my son watches
these shows and he's like

00:04:21.977 --> 00:04:25.014
Mom, can we go on a pumpkin space ride?

00:04:25.014 --> 00:04:26.097
And I'm like.

00:04:26.995 --> 00:04:30.132
And the worst show for
this is Dora the Explorer.

00:04:30.132 --> 00:04:34.175
Because she is like four and
her parents just let her wander

00:04:34.175 --> 00:04:37.162
wherever the hell she wants
and she gets to go through

00:04:37.162 --> 00:04:38.300
the forbidden forest.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.348
Oh, that's Harry Potter.

00:04:39.348 --> 00:04:43.956
She gets to go through the
magic mountain and climb trees

00:04:43.956 --> 00:04:45.035
and go off.

00:04:45.035 --> 00:04:47.150
She has like a monkey chaperone.

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:49.595
Who trusts a monkey to chaperone a child?

00:04:49.595 --> 00:04:52.440
But she's just off, off in
the world wandering around

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:55.645
from city to city just
picking up friends on the way,

00:04:55.645 --> 00:04:59.183
talking to strangers as
this weird, creepy fox

00:04:59.183 --> 00:05:00.914
trying to rob her all the time.

00:05:00.914 --> 00:05:03.446
It's like if that was my
kid I'd be like you stay

00:05:03.446 --> 00:05:04.869
the fuck inside.

00:05:04.869 --> 00:05:06.610
What are you doing going outside?

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:09.094
I don't care if this
bluebird lost its mom,

00:05:09.094 --> 00:05:10.919
it can figure its own shit out.

00:05:10.919 --> 00:05:12.706
Then my kids watch that and they're like

00:05:12.706 --> 00:05:16.065
why can't I go wander around
the neighborhood alone?

00:05:16.065 --> 00:05:18.537
Because the real world is
not like Dora the Explorer.

00:05:18.537 --> 00:05:19.617
I'm sorry, child.

00:05:19.617 --> 00:05:21.679
Why aren't there kid shows with adventures

00:05:21.679 --> 00:05:23.121
in folding the laundry?

00:05:23.121 --> 00:05:27.454
Or like drying the dishes
or Swiffering the floor?

00:05:27.454 --> 00:05:29.059
Kids are super impressionable.

00:05:29.059 --> 00:05:30.958
As long as you present
something in a cool way,

00:05:30.958 --> 00:05:31.791
they'll wanna do it.

00:05:31.791 --> 00:05:34.472
So instead of Dora the
Explorer, why isn't there like

00:05:34.472 --> 00:05:37.485
Chad, the kid who helps
out around the house.

00:05:37.485 --> 00:05:39.658
That's the kind of show
I'd like my kids to watch.

00:05:39.658 --> 00:05:40.738
Kevin, you can draw.

00:05:40.738 --> 00:05:42.883
Let's make a kids' series about cleaning.

00:05:42.883 --> 00:05:44.444
He's a really great cartoonist.

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:45.499
He's gonna do this.

00:05:45.499 --> 00:05:47.666
Kevin, can you animate it?

00:05:51.674 --> 00:05:54.022
So last, real life adults.

00:05:54.022 --> 00:05:56.554
There's something very
unsettling about adults

00:05:56.554 --> 00:06:00.368
on kids' TV shows, especially
if it's a cartoon show

00:06:00.368 --> 00:06:01.880
with a real live adult.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:04.293
Because they're adults,
but then on these shows

00:06:04.293 --> 00:06:06.369
they're pretending to be really interested

00:06:06.369 --> 00:06:09.058
in like a warm glass of milk with dinner.

00:06:09.058 --> 00:06:10.462
I'm watching this thinking no,

00:06:10.462 --> 00:06:12.969
you definitely do some
weird shit on the weekends.

00:06:12.969 --> 00:06:15.655
But the only exception is
the Wiggles and Blue's Clues,

00:06:15.655 --> 00:06:18.535
because the Wiggles are
awesome and they're super cute

00:06:18.535 --> 00:06:20.263
and the yellow one is super cute.

00:06:20.263 --> 00:06:22.450
And Steve from Blue's Clues is a babe.

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:25.290
I don't know why they
replaced him with Joe,

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:27.884
this knock-off orange shirt character.

00:06:27.884 --> 00:06:28.827
It's like orange is the
most unsettling color.

00:06:28.827 --> 00:06:29.660
Why do you have him wear this orange shirt

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:30.920
if you're wanting to get us
to appreciate a new character

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:32.408
when we've already fallen
in love with Steve.

00:06:32.408 --> 00:06:33.958
But they just bring in
Joe like guys, here's Joe,

00:06:33.958 --> 00:06:35.404
and you have like all this
weird new stuff that you do.

00:06:35.404 --> 00:06:36.919
You don't just sketch beautiful
pictures in your notebook,

00:06:36.919 --> 00:06:37.752
you do all this other weird stuff.

00:06:37.752 --> 00:06:38.959
Like Steve was just trying
to sketch nice pictures

00:06:38.959 --> 00:06:40.169
in his notebook, find the clues.

00:06:40.169 --> 00:06:41.124
It was like hide and seek, basically,

00:06:41.124 --> 00:06:42.538
and it was so awesome, and
then they bring in Joe,

00:06:42.538 --> 00:06:43.591
this new person, who's just like.

00:06:43.591 --> 00:06:44.801
Do you see what I'm doing?

00:06:44.801 --> 00:06:45.634
See what I'm doing?

00:06:45.634 --> 00:06:49.541
I'm like so into this and
it's not even a show for me.

00:06:49.541 --> 00:06:52.220
So I guess they're awful,
but they're doing their jobs

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:53.887
really, really well.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.151
Joe sucks.

00:06:57.151 --> 00:06:58.460
Steve rules.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:06:59.650
That's all I got for today.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.621
I'm Hannah, your friendly
neighborhood wine mom,

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:03.020
and if there's a show that I missed

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:05.870
that you particularly don't
like, leave it in the comments,

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:08.317
because my youngest son
is about the age to start

00:07:08.317 --> 00:07:10.459
watching TV and I need
to know what to avoid,

00:07:10.459 --> 00:07:12.809
because I'm sure there's a
new Caillou at this point.

00:07:12.809 --> 00:07:14.647
And as always, if there's
a topic you'd like me

00:07:14.647 --> 00:07:16.400
to talk about in the next episode,

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:17.578
leave that in the comments, too,

00:07:17.578 --> 00:07:20.439
because I love talking about
what you guys wanna hear.

00:07:20.439 --> 00:07:21.689
Till next time.

00:07:25.983 --> 00:07:27.733
Where's my TV remote?

